  "step_3": "The decision reason requires the individual to consider the sum of all pairwise differences of outcomes. In this case, the only difference is 1000 (4000 - 3000), and since both lotteries have the same difference magnitude, the sum is equal, and the reason would be indifferent. However, the individual does not mention any calculation of differences or their sum. Instead, the justification is rooted in emotional preferences for safety and avoiding risk, not in any analysis of outcome differences. Therefore, the individual did not use the decision reason. The information considered (risk aversion, emotional security) does not align with the required analysis of pairwise outcome differences. The justification also does not reflect the rule of the decision reason (preferring the lottery with the more favorable sum of outcome differences). Thus, the decision reason was not used.",
