  "step_3": "The decision reason requires consideration of the sum of all pairwise differences of outcomes. In this case, the pairwise differences are |5000 - 5| = 4995 and |0 - 5| = 5, summing to 5000. This sum is identical regardless of which lottery is considered, so the reason would be indifferent. However, the individual does not mention this sum or any such calculation. Instead, the justification is based solely on the low probability of the large prize, not on any analysis of outcome differences. Therefore, the individual did not use the decision reason. The information considered by the individual (low probability, small gain) is unrelated to the sum of pairwise differences. The justification is probabilistic and emotional, not based on the sum of outcome differences. Hence, the decision reason was not used.",
